From: mscharged-port native source preparation
Subject: [PATCH] Present the original VI selected completed XFB through native scanout
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: permanent native VI hardware output transport.

Carry actual flushed source VI register selection into the matching completed
GXCopyDisp GPU resource. Honor black, physical field, source pan/display geometry
and explicit virtual SC aspect records. Validate/commit outside VI locks, then
render/present after the genuine owner interrupt returns. Require actual GPU
completion and successful surface presentation; unsupported XFB/output fails.
Retain original VI callback/clock/mask/register ordering and pending cause.
No original game source, frame decisions or extra resource requests change.
Native recorder lifetime and CPU XFB writes remain independent boundaries.
Compose after exact SDK29 including native copy0028 and compiler0031.

